ARRAYS:
->An array stores multiple values in an ordered collection.

CODE: 
var fruits = ["Apple", "Mango", "Orange"]
print(fruits)----> ["Apple", "Mango", "Orange"]

ACCESSING ARRAYELEMENT:
var fruits = ["Apple", "Mango", "Orange"]
print(fruits[0])---->Apple
fruits.append("kiwi")----->["Apple", "Mango", "Orange","kiwi"]
fruits.remove("Orange")---->["Apple", "Mango","kiwi"]

//Important: Array indexing starts from 0, not 1.

DICTIONARIES:
->A dictionary stores values in key-value pairs.
Think of it like student information:
-> Key = Name
-> Value = XXXX
CODE:
var student = [
    "name": "XXXX",
    "department": "CSE",
    "college": "YYYY"
]
print(student["name"]!)----->XXXX
print(student["department"]!)---->CSE

ADDING A NEW KEY VALUE PAIRS:
var student = ["name": "XXXX"]
student["age"] = "21"
print(student)---->["age": "21", "name": "XXXX"]

